th waits)\n\n`admit()` called `self.wait_ci(h)` with `only=None`, so admission waited for **every** check at the entry head, not the merge authority's required set. Measured on a machinery-touching head this session: it waited **4+ hours** for `composed-proof` — a 180-min-cap **non-required** lane — while every required context had been green for an hour and GitHub reported `mergeStateStatus UNSTABLE`.\n\nThe same all-checks wait sat in the serial landing path: `at_head()` also waited `only=None`, and it is the one the running trains hit — measured with a faulthandler dump: `batch:1016 → one_overlap:629 → at_head:640 → wait_ci:400 (sleeping)`, at head d72be540 whose only non-completed lane was `composed-proof`. The ruleset is what blocks the merge; the settle/proof path already waited `only=req` (`required()`); admission and the head wait did not.\n\n## The fix\n\nBoth `at_head()` waits are now `self.wait_ci(h, only=req)` — `req` threaded from `batch()`'s computed `required()` list (admission, the landing loop's `one`/`one_overlap`), with the `run` command path computing it once per entry inside `one()` the same way. Nothing else changes: a red **required** context still raises `Stop(\"ci\")` at either site; the `--ignore-red` filter still applies to the judged names; exit codes unchanged. The settle/proof waits are untouched.\n\n## Self-test arms\n\n- **admission concludes while a non-required lane is pending**: a new stub lane (`composed-proof`, `in_progress` forever at PR heads) no longer holds a batch — both entries merge, rc 0.\n- **a red required context still stops admission**: `policy-docs` red at the PR heads stops with `Stop(\"ci\")`, nothing pushed or merged.\n- **`--overlap`'s `at_head` wait concludes while `composed-proof` stays in_progress at the head**: the serial landing (`one_overlap`, the path the faulthandler traced) merges all three entries, rc 0.\n- Four existing arms re-cut only where they asserted the old all-checks behavior: the red-required arms at both sites now use a required context's failure (`fast`), the min-runs arm pins that the required-only wait no longer applies `--min-runs` (the required set is complete below it), and the never-dispatched required-context TIMEOUT now lands at admission itself, before any proof is spent.\n\nFull `merge_train.py --self-test`: 111 checks, 0 failed. `tests/structure.py`: ratchet passed, no budget raised.\n\n## Gate\n\n`tools/audit/seat` is not code-owned; the `hpo-author` App approval suffices per the orchestrator's standing verdict plan.\n\n## Mutation proof\n\nn/a: no behavioral branch to kill — the change selects which check names a single existing wait judges; the arms above pin the selection both ways (a stuck non-required lane admits at both sites, a red required stops at both), and the CI stub's pending/in_progress clock is the perturbation the first and third arms fail under the old `only=None` code.\n\n## Null control\n\nn/a: the pending-lane arms are the null controls — a world whose only difference is a never-concluding non-required lane merges exactly as the clean world does, and the untouched settle/proof `only=req` arms still pass unchanged.\n\n## Figures\n\n- `python3 tools/audit/seat/merge_train.py --self-test` → `merge_train self-test: 111 checks, 0 failed`\n- `python3 tests/structure.py` → `STRUCTURE RATCHET PASSED` (max_method_loc 373 <= 373, methods_over_200 9 <= 9)\n\n## Red checks\n\n- `closures`, `closures-autofix`, `pr-contract` at 9d0edb108: the main-side composed-verify stdout defect (job 115038269065's cp line), answered by #2164, merged on main at c613d0005 — this branch's post-update head carries the fix and the train's recarry re-fires the lanes on it.\n\nnone: the checks run here are the tool's own self-test and the structure ratchet, both green; no red remains on this head.\n\n## Forward-carry\n\nnone: no later stage's behavior changes — the orchestrator's merge_train invocation and every other seat's contract are unchanged.\n\n## Friction\n\nunclear: cost: `git add tools/audit/seat/merge_train.py` was refused by a `.gitignore` rule against the directory even though the file is tracked (it was already staged; the refusal only aborted the compound command). Worth a look some quiet day; not this PR.\n\n","created_at":"2026-10-13T08:02:44Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T13:42:21Z","closed_at":"2026-10-13T13:42:19Z","merged_at":"2026-10-13T13:42:19Z","merge_commit_sha":"96901a0d902bd604e2caf02a7b54222d7f9a31c4","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2170/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2170/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2170/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/statuses/7f3fc32cbf55dbbcb6d8e6122037c1536c1c041d","head":{"label":"tvofi:fix/admit-wait-required","ref":"fix/admit-wait-required","sha":"7f3fc32cbf55dbbcb6d8e6122037c1536c1c041d","user":{"login":"tvofi","id":70032254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMDMyMjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/events{/privacy}","received_even